# Three inputs, two outputs, and one command that is also the check. The point of the shape is
# that nothing a person writes and nothing a program produces ever share a file.

title How a blueprint is put together

size 980 620

box gen 40 70 280 100 "generate.cs" "a program whose output" "is markdown, not numbers"
box src 350 70 280 100 "blueprint.src.md" "the sections a person writes," "with holes in them"
box man 660 70 280 100 "blueprint.json" "id, status, and the" "list of sources"

box tool 350 230 280 90 "xray build blueprints" "runs it, then fills the holes"

box out 40 390 280 100 "generated/*.md" "committed, and compared" "on every pull request"
box page 350 390 280 100 "blueprint.md" "the document, front matter" "and header included"

note chk 660 390 280 100 "xray check blueprints" "the same code with one flag" "flipped, so a stale file fails"

arrow gen tool
arrow src tool
arrow man tool
arrow tool out
arrow tool page
